# Backend API Architecture

## Stack
*   Node.js `"type": "module"` — import/export only.
*   Express 4, mounted at `/trips/`.
*   Sequelize 6 + mysql2; config in `app/config/db.config.js` via dotenv.
*   Separate `sequelizeInstance.js`; models import it and register in `models/index.js`.
*   bcryptjs + jsonwebtoken + Session model for auth.
*   winston + morgan (morgan streams to winston).
*   multer for image/document uploads; static mounts for `/trips/images` and `/trips/uploads`.

## server.js Responsibilities
*   `db.sequelize.sync()` on startup (skipped when `NODE_ENV=test`); optional `{ alter: true }` when `SEQUELIZE_SYNC_ALTER=true`; then `ensureSchema()` when syncing.
*   CORS with `credentials: true` and frontend origin (`CORS_ORIGIN` or `http://localhost:8082`).
*   `express.json()` and `urlencoded({ extended: true })`.
*   Mount routes: `app.use("/trips", routes)`.
*   Export `app` as default; call `listen()` only when `NODE_ENV !== "test"`.

## Route Layout
*   `app/routes/index.js` — central router registering each `*.routes.js`.
*   Auth at mount root: `POST /login`, `POST /register`, `POST /logout`, `GET /me`, `POST /change-password`, `POST /reset-password` (dev only), `GET /register/organizations`.
*   Resource routers: `/people`, `/organizations`, `/trips`, `/donations`, `/public`, etc.
*   Public unauthenticated surface: `/public/*` (see ADR-0004).

Trips REST examples (full paths under `/trips`):
*   `POST /trips/login`, `POST /trips/register`
*   `GET/POST /trips/trips`, `GET /trips/trips/browse/:id`
*   `GET /trips/public/trips/by-name/:tripSlug`

## Controller Pattern
```javascript
import db from "../models/index.js";
import logger from "../config/logger.js";

const exports = {};
exports.findAll = async (req, res) => { /* ... */ };
export default exports;
```
*   Parse route IDs: `parseInt(req.params.id, 10)`; reject `NaN`.
*   Use `logger.debug/warn/error` — never `console.log`.
*   Sequelize `include` for associations; `order` for stable list sorting.
*   Prefer `optimisticUpdate` for versioned entities (ADR-0005).

## JSON Responses
*   **Success:** `res.send(data)` or `res.status(201).send(created)`.
*   **Failure:** `res.status(4xx).send({ message: "Human-readable explanation." })`.
*   Do **not** use `{ success, data }` envelopes.

## Model Conventions
*   Sensitive fields excluded via `defaultScope` (e.g. User password).
*   Use `Model.unscoped()` only when password compare is required at login.
*   Associations and `hasMany`/`belongsTo` defined in `models/index.js`, not scattered in controllers.

## Schema Changes
Incremental scripts in `app/scripts/` — one concern per file (`ensureSchema.js`, `seedRoles.js`), runnable via npm scripts.

## Protected Routes
```javascript
import { authenticate } from "../authorization/accessControl.js";

router.get("/", [authenticate], controller.findAll);
```
`authenticate` looks up Bearer token in Session table, checks expiration, loads person/org/trip roles onto `req.user`.
